In Snowflake Inc., compute is billed per second with a 60-second minimum each time the warehouse resumes.

Question 1: 

An X-SMALL virtual warehouse has AUTO_SUSPEND = 300 seconds and AUTO_RESUME = TRUE.
A user executes a query that runs for 1 minute. No additional queries are submitted after the query completes.
How long will compute credits be billed for this warehouse?

A. 1 minute
B. 5 minutes
C. 6 minutes
D. Only the 60-second minimum billing period


Ans: 

-- Query runtime (1 min) + Idle time before auto-suspend (5 min) = 6 minutes



I started my vwh, it is running state, after 2 minutes, I submit a query, it runs for a minute, then what is the cost?

Ans: 

--2 min (pre-query idle)+1 min (query)+5 min (post-query idle)=8 minutes total


I started my vwh, it is running state, after 2 minutes 20 seconds, I submit a query, it runs for a minute, then what is the cost?

Ans: 
--2 min 20 sec+1 min+5 min=8 min 20 sec


Question 1: 

A user creates a new Virtual Warehouse in Snowflake.

At the moment of creation, before starting the warehouse, how much compute cost will be incurred?

A. Full hourly cost based on warehouse size
B. Pro-rated cost until the first query is executed
C. No compute cost
D. Minimum 60-second billing

Ans: 

In Snowflake, compute is billed only when a warehouse is in the RUNNING state.
Creating a warehouse does not start it automatically (unless you explicitly resume or start it).
Billing begins when the warehouse runs queries or is manually/resumed started.


