Question: 

How the storage cost is calculated? if I have used only 500 GB of data (uncompressed) for a month?

Ans: 

Snowflake storage is charged based on, compressed data size stored per month (in TB)

Storage Cost=(Average Compressed TB)×Price per TB

Time Travel / Fail-safe adds extra storage cost.

Snowflake storage pricing is:
=============================

	Charged per TB per month

	Calculated daily (average storage per day)

	Based on compressed size, NOT raw/uncompressed size
	
In Snowflake, Typical compression ratio = 2x to 5x (depends on data type), Let’s assume average 3x compression.

hence, 500 GB÷3= 167 GB = 0.167 TB

lets assume, ~$23 per TB per month (Standard edition)

Ans: 0.167×23≈$3.84 per month


