Scenario 1: 

Warehouse: XSMALL, 1 credit/hour

Query activity:

Daily ETL load: 30 minutes per day

Ad-hoc analytics queries: 15 minutes per day

Warehouse auto-suspends after 60 seconds idle

Data Storage:

Raw data ingested daily: 200 GB uncompressed

Compression ratio: ~3x (typical for Snowflake)

Retention: 30 days of historical data


Compute Cost Calculation: 
=========================

1) Total Warehouse Running Time

	Daily ETL: 30 min = 1800 sec

	Ad-hoc queries: 15 min = 900 sec

	Auto-suspend overhead: negligible (assume warehouse suspends immediately after last query for simplicity)

	Total daily running time = 1800 + 900 = 2700 sec = 0.75 hours

2)Compute Credits Used

	Credits Used = Warehouse Size Factor × Seconds Used /3600

	Credits Used= 1 x 2700/3600 = 0.75 credits per day

3)Monthly Compute Cost

	Assume 22 working days/month then 0.75 × 22 = 16.5 credits/month

	If Snowflake credit cost = $3.50 per credit then 16.5 × 3.50 = $57.75 / month for compute


Storage Cost Calculation:
=========================

1) Compressed Data Size

	Daily data ingestion: 200 GB uncompressed

	Compression ratio: 3x = 200 %3 ~ 67 GB per day (compressed)

	Retention: 30 days, 67×30 ~ 2,010 GB ~ 2 TB

2) Storage Cost

	Snowflake storage cost = $23 per TB per month

	2 TB×23 ~ $46/month
